Notes (honest disclosure — no silent drift):
  - i18n catalog generator: res/values*/strings.xml is AUTO-GENERATED by
    apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts. The COMMITTED catalog is ALREADY
    DRIFTED from the current web/src/i18n/en.json before this change: every
    committed key carries a `translation_` prefix (e.g.
    translation_settingsSessions_title), but the current en.json has NO top-level
    `translation` wrapper, so a fresh gen run would emit un-prefixed names — i.e.
    the committed catalog was generated from an older wrapped en.json and is stale
    (none of the existing keys round-trip to the current en.json; verified
    programmatically). The web ActiveSessionsPage carries account.sessions.title /
    .subtitle only as inline t(key, default) FALLBACKS (no en.json key today), so
    there is no en.json source row to mirror. Editing en.json is also outside this
    artifact's allowed files. The two Android keys were therefore named + placed to
    match the committed catalog's own convention exactly: prefix `translation_` +
    the dot-path `settings.account.sessions.{title,subtitle}` underscored
    (androidName transform), inserted in the generator's sorted position. A future
    full gen-i18n run that re-introduces these keys at the en.json source re-emits
    the same names (no conflict). The section's own keys
    (translation_settingsSessions_*) already exist and were not touched.
  - SI: no session field is unit-bearing (id, user-agent, IP, ISO stamps, current
    flag) — no SI conversion; timestamp localization is the feature view's render
    boundary (S5).
  - States: ActiveSessionsSection renders loading / open-mode advisory / content /
    empty(no rows) / hard-error+retry / stale-offline for its bound feed (the page
    drives the feed through the shared SessionsStore + asUiState projection).
  - i18n: every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept
    (account.sessions.title/subtitle -> translation_settings_account_sessions_*).
  - a11y: PageTitle heading + copy-link IconButton contentDescription; the feature
    view supplies the row revoke aria-label, the device badge, the confirm dialogs,
    and dynamic/dark theme (ADR-015).
  - Layout: the feature view composes as a non-lazy Column, so it nests safely
    inside the page's outer verticalScroll container.

